       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g/day, which is above the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. That's a risk of hepatotoxicity even with normal liver function. A single 2000 mg dose is also higher than the standard 500\u20131000 mg.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day). This is a common standard order.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day). This is the usual maximum for a 70 kg adult. Many institutions cap at 3 g/day for safety.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day).\n\nDid you mean one of these, perhaps 1000 mg instead of 2000 mg? If 2000 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me the clinical reason and I'll go from there. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
